{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":145665,"duration_api_ms":189953,"num_turns":9,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6a960de3-844d-4571-9ca0-ae240d1b5876","total_cost_usd":0.58236245,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29902,"cache_read_input_tokens":237542,"output_tokens":3156,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29902,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":135,"outputTokens":7962,"cacheReadInputTokens":737727,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67237,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.19776395000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":3156,"cacheReadInputTokens":237542,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29902,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.38459850000000007,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept all four hardcoded-constant amendments (fr-7-65339123, fr-7-dd2544eb, fr-7-96901ca8, fr-7-b39b6c90) as they are verified real violations of the acceptance criteria requiring named parameters. Accept all three probe-robustness amendments (fr-7-63a03cd8, fr-7-7ca6ed81, fr-7-e444967f) as they identify genuine test quality issues. Reject the snapshot-field amendment (fr-7-1cbde9f3) because TankSnapshot already carries recent_events with detailed MoltFailure and MoltStressWarning events including cause codes and summaries, satisfying the observability requirement.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-7-65339123","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the 0.6 threshold at shrimp.rs:1411 is hardcoded in `emit_molt_stress_warning` and controls when MoltStressWarning events fire. ShrimpRuntimeParams already has many molt-related named parameters (molt_success_threshold, critical_molt_gh_ratio, etc.), but this threshold is conspicuously absent. The acceptance criteria explicitly require all molt-related thresholds to be named parameters, making this a clear violation."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-dd2544eb","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the mineral stress blend weights (0.5/0.3/0.2 at line 480), stress pressure weights (lines 493-497), and exponential smoothing constants (rise=0.2 at line 502, decay=0.05 at line 504) are all hardcoded. These constants define the core transfer function from mineral deficits into molt_stress_index — the central signal of the molt mechanics. They are behavior-shaping modifiers, not incidental implementation constants, and belong alongside the other molt parameters already in ShrimpRuntimeParams."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-96901ca8","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the 0.5 subtraction at shrimp.rs:1196 in `compute_mortality_probabilities` is a hardcoded activation threshold that determines when molt stress begins contributing to mortality. This is functionally equivalent to molt_success_threshold or similar named parameters already in ShrimpRuntimeParams. Since it directly affects the lethality boundary, it needs to be tunable and explicit."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-b39b6c90","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the 10.0 divisor at shrimp.rs:1679 shapes the GH-excess penalty curve, and the 0.3 floor clamp at lines 1684 and 1689 sets the minimum Ca/Mg contribution under deficiency. These are biologically meaningful curve parameters that determine how mineral imbalances translate into molt outcomes. ShrimpRuntimeParams already contains ca_min_mg_per_l and mg_min_mg_per_l but lacks the penalty curve shaping constants, which should be co-located."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-1cbde9f3","decision":"reject","rationale":"TankSnapshot already exposes `recent_events` (last 20 SimEvents), and both MoltFailure and MoltStressWarning events include detailed cause_codes (HighGH, LowCalcium, LowMagnesium, WaterInstability, TemperatureStress, LowReserves, PoorCondition, MarginalFailure) and human-readable summaries with specific GH/Ca/Mg values and scores. This satisfies the acceptance criterion that 'events, tracing, or snapshots expose enough detail to explain why molt failure occurred.' Adding raw internal state fields would be a nice-to-have but is not a correctness or acceptance-criteria gap."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-63a03cd8","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: `all_habitat_geometry_probes_summary` calls the exact same `run_probe_*` functions that are invoked by standalone #[test] wrapper functions. The artifact_dir is deterministically derived from scenario_id, artifact_label, and seed (lib.rs:624-640), so parallel test execution can produce two runs writing to the same temp directory simultaneously. This is a real race condition that can corrupt failure artifacts needed for debugging. The fix is straightforward: either deduplicate the invocations or use distinct artifact labels in the summary test."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-7ca6ed81","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the light-depth probe at line 654 only asserts `growth_shallow > growth_deep`. With both values negative (shallow=-0.4029g, deep=-0.7110g), the probe passes while neither tank actually grew plant biomass. The documented purpose is to verify 'more plant biomass growth' in shallow tanks, which implies positive growth. The assertion should require at least the shallow tank to exhibit non-negative growth, or the probe cannot distinguish 'light helps growth' from 'light slows decline.'"},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-e444967f","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: at lines 305-321, nitrifier biomass is seeded as `carrying_capacity * INITIAL_CAPACITY_FRACTION`, where carrying_capacity depends on filter-media area. The larger-media run starts with proportionally more nitrifier biomass before any dynamics run, so the assertions checking lower reduced-N exposure and higher final biomass are partially tautological. The probe should either seed identical initial biomass in both runs (testing colonization/growth advantage from more surface area) or explicitly account for the proportional seeding in its assertions."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2ca72399-cd83-466f-9a88-5bdcf6ffbc2a"}
